  "summary": "A multistage macOS phishing campaign delivers AppleScript lures masquerading as Microsoft documents that exfiltrate credentials to sevrrhst[.]com and attempt to forge TCC authorizations for Apple-signed binaries before dropping a modular Node.js loader with LaunchAgent persistence. The same report documents CikaBika Bot, a Rust RAT unpacked by a Nim loader from a disk-image lure that hijacks Edge's delay-loaded dbghelp.dll and uses Discord channels plus ngrok for C2 and exfiltration. Detection anchors include the AppleScript/TCC artifacts (dscl -authonly, codesign -d --requirements, csreq, killall tccd, ~/.ex.scpt, ~/.nodes, com.appled.tcc) and the Edge dbghelp.dll plant plus Discord !shell command strings.",
